SUMMARY:Saturday Freethought Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n**July 11 Discussion Guide**\n\
 n**Reason: How do we know what we know?**\nReason is not the absence of fe
 eling.\nIt is the practice of testing what we believe against evidence\, l
 ogic\, experience\, and correction.\n\nReason asks:\n**How did I get this 
 idea? What supports it? What might change my mind?**\n\n**Ground Rules:**\
 nTimed rounds\n\n* Up to 2 minutes each\n* Option to pass\n* No interrupti
 ons\n* Brief open discussion after each round\n\n**Q1 - Your personal star
 ting point**\nWhat is something you believe strongly\, and how did you com
 e to believe it?\n\n**Q2 - Evidence**\nWhat kind of evidence do you trust 
 most: lived experience\, science\, history\, experts\, patterns\, or logic
 ?\n\n**Q3 - Bias**\nHow do emotion\, identity\, loyalty\, or fear shape wh
 at we think we know?\n\n**Q4 - Revision**\nWhen have you changed your mind
 \, and what made that possible?\n\n**Closing Q -** What is one reasoning h
 abit you want to strengthen?\n\n**Come curious. Come ready to listen.**\n\
 nAfter this event\, you're welcome to continue on with us to dinner at the
  Indian Curry Lounge. Please RSVP for dinner at 6 pm here - https://www.me
 etup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/315441869/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 315485464/
